Authentic leaked documents from a $250 million Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) public health campaign, obtained by Politico, revealed a vetting process used to exclude celebrities who criticized President Trump ([W Magazine](https://www.wmagazine.com/story/trump-campaign-celebrity-rapper-endorsements), [Vulture](https://www.vulture.com/2020/10/trump-administration-approved-celebrities-covid-ad.html)). While some reports claimed the administration accused Billie Eilish of "destroying our country" ([Yahoo Money](https://money.yahoo.com/leaked-trump-admin-document-describes-191559664.html)), the leaked "PSA Celebrity Tracker" actually quoted Eilish's own words from the August 2020 Democratic National Convention, where she stated that Donald Trump "is destroying our country and everything we care about" ([NY Post](https://nypost.com/2020/10/30/washington-post-wrongly-claims-trump-officials-criticized-billie-eilish/)). The document recorded her statement to note she was "not a Trump supporter" as grounds for her exclusion from the campaign ([Happy Mag](https://happymag.tv/leaked-trump-docs-billie-eilish-destroying-america/)). Therefore, the claim is refuted because the phrase was a quote of Eilish criticizing Trump, not an administration accusation against her.